James asked about using his wife's domain `matchedbyjo.com` to display content from `https://matchedbyjo.my.canva.site/matched-by-jo`, while hiding the original URL. I explained two methods: URL redirection and reverse proxy, recommending the latter to maintain the display of `matchedbyjo.com`. I provided detailed instructions for setting up a reverse proxy on either Apache or Nginx web servers. James then inquired whether this could be done on DreamHost, and I confirmed that it was possible on VPS or dedicated server plans, but not on shared hosting. I reiterated the steps required for both Apache and Nginx, including optional SSL configuration, and suggested testing the setup after configuration.
